   677	//    destructor, sync_and_release_all_impl, recycle_event) no longer allocate, except the pending-list push in the
   678	//    destructor, which is caught and falls back to a synchronous release (counted). sync_and_release_all_impl works on
   679	//    the live list in place (phase 1 synchronizes the devices into a fixed-capacity set, phase 2 pops completed
   680	//    entries), instead of a take-all std::deque swap and a std::set / std::vector of devices, which allocated inside a
