docs/P1T_REV_REPORT.md:180:M1 says the late/already-finalized interpreter guard leaks instead of crashing, but does not test finalization in progress. Its published no-drain mutant survived Voice G1, while a corrected own test caught it; this narrows what G1 proves. M2 explicitly discloses unenforced nonlegacy lifetime requirements and multi-GPU untested status. M3 confirms the second handle is a scope deviation and cuBLAS workspace allocation exception; neither fact alone establishes a kernel race. M3/M4 also report an own-suite allocator-test failure rather than a completely clean suite. These observations do not change independently derived F01-F05.
